sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-tame-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Problem-solving behaviour of animals in three-dimensional space is proposed to be a variant of an evolutionarily more ancient capacity to solve problems in metabolic, physiological, transcriptional and morphogenetic spaces.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Behavioural problem-solving in 3D space derives from older problem-solving in other spaces";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: An Experimentally-Grounded Framework for Understanding Diverse Bodies and Minds”, Frontiers in systems neuroscience (2022), doi:10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201; section “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: A Proposal for a Framework › Specific Conceptual Components of the Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere Framework”. Scope: Evolution of problem-solving capacities across life"
}
